      },
      "rubricNotes": "Turn 1 must list 5 orders from the store. Turn 2 should filter — correctness includes not re-listing unshipped orders. Tool-call bound tightened 2026-04-23 after both HEAD runs landed n=1 on each turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "orders_with_email",
      "category": "read",
      "scope": "GLOBAL",
      "smokeFixture": null,
      "turns": [
        {
          "userMessage": "Get order list with customer emails",
          "hardChecks": [
            {
              "type": "TOOL_CALLED",
              "value": "orders_list"
            },
            {
              "type": "TOOL_CALLED_ANY",
              "value": "show_cards"
            },
            {
              "type": "TOTAL_TOOL_CALL_COUNT_AT_MOST",
              "value": "4"
            },
            {
              "type": "ASSISTANT_TEXT_CONTAINS_ANY",
              "value": "@|tap|open the order|see the email|billing detail|order detail"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "userMessage": "how many of them come from the same customer?",
          "hardChecks": []
        }
      ],
      "hardChecks": [
        {
          "type": "TOTAL_TOOL_CALL_COUNT_AT_MOST",
          "value": "12"
        },
        {
          "type": "ASSISTANT_TEXT_NOT_CONTAINS",
          "value": "wp-admin"
        },
        {
          "type": "ASSISTANT_TEXT_NOT_CONTAINS",
          "value": "wp admin"
        },
        {
          "type": "ASSISTANT_TEXT_NOT_CONTAINS",
          "value": "dashboard"
        },
        {
          "type": "ASSISTANT_TEXT_NOT_CONTAINS",
          "value": "dashboards"
        }
      ],
      "iosHard": {
        "t1": {
          "required_tools": [
            "orders_list"
          ],
          "required_tools_any": [
            "show_cards"
          ],
          "max_tool_calls": 4,
          "text_must_contain_any": [
            "@",
            "tap",
            "open the order",
            "see the email",
            "billing detail",
            "order detail"
          ]
        }
      },
      "rubricNotes": "OrdersListSummary doesn't carry billing_email, so the only paths to email are (a) orders_list + show_cards then point the merchant at the card/native UI for the email, or (b) bounded fanout via orders_get for a few rows. Both are valid - what's NOT acceptable is fabricating email addresses. The text invariant accepts either an actual '@' surfaced from a card/get OR a polite pointer to tap/open the order. Turn 2 tests whether the model reuses turn-1 data."
    },
